Basic Data Structures
Objects
An object is a basic data structure that stores data
Student stu = new Student("Ahmed", 1234);
One-Dimensional Array
Array of primitive data types (array of integers, doubles, etc.)
int[] arr = new int[10];
Array of objects
Student[] students = new Student[5];
Multi-Dimensional Array
Example: two-dimensional array with 20 rows and 5 columns
double[][] = new double[20][5];
